{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: vendored-fork divergence now undocumented**

Renaming `undoStack` → `_undoStack` silently breaks this file's own sync invariant. The header still states:

> Otherwise byte-identical to the fork source; keep in sync when the fork editor changes.

But `vendor/dart_tui/lib/src/editor.dart` still declares the **public** `undoStack` field — the fork and this copy now diverge, and nothing marks the deviation as deliberate. The next "re-sync from the fork" edit will copy the public field back over, reintroducing the `library_private_types_in_public_api` INFO (which CI now fails on).

The new `--fatal-infos` gate does catch the lint regression, so this is not blocking — but please add one line to the header noting the deliberate deviation, e.g.:

```dart
// DEVIATES from the fork: undoStack is _undoStack here (private-field
// formal; vendored fork exposes the _UndoStep-typed field publicly) —
// gh-1547. Keep this rename when re-syncing from the fork.
```

That keeps the sync contract honest without needing an `// ignore:`.
